.TH "SLIPWAY-MAN" "1" "2026-09-30" "slipway 0.1.0" "Slipway Manual"
.SH NAME
slipway\-man \- Show the manual page of a command
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY "slipway man"
.RI [ COMMAND... ]\&
.RI [ flags ]
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
Show the manual page of slipway or of one of its commands with man(1).
The pages ship with the gem; \-\-install copies them into a man1 directory and says how man(1) finds them.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-path\fR
Print the directory of the bundled pages and exit.
.TP
\fB\-\-install\fR[=\fIDIR\fR]
Copy every page into DIR, a man1 directory, or into ${XDG_DATA_HOME:\-~/.local/share}/man/man1.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
# Read the page of a command
slipway man get
.EE
.PP
.EX
# Install every page for man(1)
slipway man \-\-install
.EE
.PP
.EX
# Print the bundled page directory
slipway man \-\-path
.EE
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR slipway (1)
